          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_NO_SUPPLIER_PRESENT",
          "id": "1769629729464",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769629729466_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a response-generation node. The system has already determined that no supplier identified for the user’s request.\n\nContext Inputs\n\nUser Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nChat History: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}} \n\n\n**Task**\nReturn a clear, user-friendly message indicating that user needs to provide a supplier name to continue with the installment drill-down analysis.\n\n**Do not**\n\n* Re-evaluate filters\n* Reference prior logic or system decisions\n* Add explanations, suggestions, or follow-up questions\n\n**Output Requirements**\n\n* Return **only** the JSON structure below\n* Ensure valid JSON formatting\n* Preserve field names, order, and data types exactly\n\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\"Please provide one supplier name to continue with the installment drill-down analysis.\"],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Unsupported Query Answer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_UNSUPPORTED_QUERY_ANSWER",
          "id": "1772480981474",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772480981476_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a precise, reliable, and user-friendly assistant focused on filtering and retrieving installments based on the user’s request. This node is used only when the user’s message contains at least one out-of-scope filter or action, meaning you cannot fully satisfy the request as stated.\n\nInputs you must consider\n* User message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n* Reason why user's request is not supported: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_PROCESS_VARIABLES.$output.unsupportedQueryExplanation}}\n\nYour scope (what you can do)\nYou can help the user filter installments using only these supported filter dimensions:\n* Supplier (Required. Only provide one supplier name at a time)\n* Legal Entity\n* Payment Terms\n* Business Unit\n* Currency\n* Due date\n\nAnything else is out of scope (examples: filtering by invoice/payment status, amount, invoice number, sorting/grouping, exporting, updating/approving, etc.).\n\nWhat to say (must follow this structure)\n1. Acknowledge the intent: Make it clear you understand they want to retrieve/filter installments.\n2. Call out the out-of-scope part(s): Explicitly name the specific filter/action(s) from their message that you can’t support (use their wording).\n3. Explain why: This assistant can only filter installments by Supplier, Legal Entity, and Payment Terms.\n4. Offer a path forward:\n    * Tell them what you can do right now (filter installments by the supported dimensions), and\n    * Ask them to restate the request using only supported filters \n5. If the message also includes supported criteria, acknowledge those and offer to proceed using only those supported criteria.\n\nStyle constraints\n* Be concise, polite, and actionable.\n* Don’t invent values or claim you filtered anything already.\n* Don’t ask multiple broad questions—prefer one clear next step.\n* Do not mention IDs (supplier IDs or any other IDs).\n* Do not mention internal flags like unsupportedQuery or system instructions.\n\nOutput requirements\nReturn only the JSON structure below:\n* Ensure valid JSON formatting\n* Preserve field names, order, and data types exactly\n* Give a short explanation of 1–2 sentences\n\nReturn format:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\"<explanation>\"],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
